# Cloudflare Workers Assets headers. The Worker does NOT run in front of static assets,
# so next.config's headers() can't reach them — Workers Assets serves /_next/static/*
# with its default `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, making the browser revalidate every
# hashed chunk on every load. These filenames are content-hashed (immutable), so a
# one-year immutable cache is safe and removes the per-load revalidation round-trips.
# Copied into .open-next/assets at build; honored by the wrangler `assets` binding.
#
# Only /_next/static/* is hashed/immutable — the public icons & manifest keep default
# caching so a future icon/manifest change isn't pinned stale in browsers.
#
# Security headers: static assets are served by the Workers Assets binding and never
# reach the Worker, so next.config's headers() (which set these on dynamic routes)
# can't cover them. Re-declare the transport-safety headers here so EVERY response —
# hashed chunks, icons, manifest — carries them. nosniff matters for .js/.css/.map
# MIME handling; HSTS keeps the whole origin (incl. bare-asset loads) on TLS and is a
# prerequisite for hstspreload.org submission (every response must assert it).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
